<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sellasia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/222-bce">222 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenean-war">Cleomenean War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sellasia was fought in 222 BCE north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-iii-doson">Antigonus III Doson</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and the Achaean League defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleomenes-iii">Cleomenes III</a> of Sparta. Cleomenes fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, Sparta was occupied by a foreign army for the first time, and his reforms were reversed. The victory restored Macedonian dominance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sellasia.jpg" alt="Battle of Sellasia" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Semperf · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SouthernPeloponessus.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
